.TH mergeblockmap "1" "" "The scalpel3 Blockmap Merger" "The scalpel3 Blockmap Merger"

.SH NAME
mergeblockmap \- Merge multiple scalpel3 blockmaps into one

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mergeblockmap
\fIoutput_file\fR
\fIimage_file\fR
\fIblockmap_file1\fR
[\fIblockmap_file2\fR ...]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBmergeblockmap\fR combines coverage from one or more scalpel3 blockmaps
after windowed carving. Input blockmaps must have identical block sizes and
block counts, and their active carve windows must not overlap.
.PP
The \fIimage_file\fR argument specifies the disk image that the blockmaps
refer to.  All input blockmaps must have been created from the same
image.
.PP
Coverage is copied only from each input's active window. The output window
extends from the smallest starting block to the largest ending block;
gaps between input windows are initially uncovered. Duplicate and zero
block information is recalculated over the combined window using the image.
.PP
\fIoutput_file\fR is overwritten if it exists. Use a separate output path
that does not name the image or an input blockmap.

.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns zero on success and nonzero for incompatible inputs, overlapping
windows, or read/write failures.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR scalpel3 (1),
.BR crblockmap (1),
.BR modblockmap (1),
.BR cmpblockmaps (1),
.BR mergecps (1)

